  "body": "@johannhof and I have been looking at [cookie layering](https://github.com/httpwg/http-extensions/issues/2084), i.e., a refactoring of the Cookie RFC. One of the things that would be useful is to be able to refer to a URL path as its own concept, similar to how you can refer to a URL path segment today.\r\n\r\n(I think we only need list-based URL paths, but it seems okay for the concept to encompass both. Perhaps other cookie clients want to support non-HTTP(S) schemes in some manner.)",
